# LeakSanitizer suppressions for greycat-pro test runs.
#
# Everything here is a THIRD-PARTY / SYSTEM one-shot leak, NOT greycat code.
# All are process-lifetime allocations made once at Vulkan backend init and
# never freed by design; they do not grow with the number of tests.
#
# Use:  LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=$PWD/script/lsan.supp <asan greycat> test
#
# --- bundled ggml Vulkan backend (lib/ai/libggml-vulkan.so) ---------------
# ggml_backend_vk_reg_get_device() stores `new ggml_backend_vk_device_context`
# and `new ggml_backend_device` in a function-local `static std::vector` that
# has no destructor -> one device-context per GPU, intentionally never freed.
leak:ggml_backend_vk_reg_get_device
leak:libggml-vulkan.so
#
# --- D-Bus connection state pulled in by Vulkan device enumeration --------
# The Vulkan loader/driver queries the system bus while enumerating GPUs;
# libdbus caches connection/message-loader state for the life of the process.
leak:libdbus-1.so
leak:dbus_*
leak:_dbus_*
